// src/v4/extdeps/process.dag
//
// Scope: process model — child process invocation, lifecycle, exit codes, signals.
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Process_(computing)
//         (POSIX/SUS process model — fork/exec/wait, exit codes, signal handling)
//
// Owns:
//   - Process { id, command, state, parent }
//     (NO separate exit_code field — termination status lives ONLY inside
//     ProcessState::Exited(ExitCode). A separate exit_code would allow
//     Running-with-exit-code or Exited(0)-but-exit_code=1 — illegal states
//     representable. The state sum is the single source of truth; exit
//     code is reached via pattern-match on state.)
//   - ProcessId (PID, PositiveInt — never zero per POSIX)
//   - ProcessState = Running | Exited(ExitCode) | Signaled(SignalNum)
//   - ExitCode = NonNegativeInt (per POSIX — 0 success, 1-255 conventional)
//   - SignalNum (per POSIX signal table)
//   - Command { program: AbsolutePath, args: List<String>, env: Map<String,String> }
//   - spawn(cmd) -> Result<Process, Diagnostic>     (fork+exec)
//   - wait(p)    -> Result<ExitCode, Diagnostic>    (blocks until terminated)
//   - capture(p) -> Result<{stdout, stderr, exit}, Diagnostic>  (read pipes + wait)
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/diagnostic.dag: Diagnostic
//   - std/primitive.dag: Int, String + their totalizations
//   - std/collection.dag: List, Map
//   - extdeps/file_system.dag: AbsolutePath (for Command.program)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-4.5
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.extdeps.process

